137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (Flooding is a recurring natural hazard in the Brahmaputra Basin of Assam, causing extensive damage to lives, agriculture, and infrastructure. Accurate flood susceptibility mapping is essential for effective risk management and planning. Machine Learning techniques have been widely used to model complex, nonlinear relationships in geospatial flood data, offering improved predictive capabilities. Recently, Quantum Machine Learning has emerged as a novel paradigm, potentially enhancing learning through quantum feature representations. This study explores and compares classical and quantum models for flood susceptibility mapping.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
